---
import SectionNav from './SectionNav.astro';
import MetroTimeline from './metro/MetroTimeline.astro';
import MetroNetworkGrow from './metro/MetroNetworkGrow.astro';
import MetroRules from './metro/MetroRules.astro';
import MetroSwap from './metro/MetroSwap.astro';
import MetroVia5 from './metro/MetroVia5.astro';
import MetroWorks from './metro/MetroWorks.astro';
import MetroTbm from './metro/MetroTbm.astro';
import MetroSlip from './metro/MetroSlip.astro';
import MetroAnatomy from './metro/MetroAnatomy.astro';
import MetroA3Layers from './metro/MetroA3Layers.astro';
import MetroLoop from './metro/MetroLoop.astro';
import MetroValles from './metro/MetroValles.astro';
import { LINES } from './metro/lines';

const changelog = [
  { date: '21 Jun 2022', title: 'First edition', items: [['+', 'Boring machine box, with its speed'], ['+', 'Tunnel statistics panel'], ['+', 'Opening years from the PDI 2021–2030']] },
  { date: 'Mar 2023', title: 'Progress only', items: [['~', 'Tunnel redrawn up to Sarrià'], ['~', 'Nothing else changes, not even the statistics']] },
  { date: 'Apr 2023', title: 'New names', items: [['~', 'La Bonanova → Mandri'], ['~', 'Parc Güell → Muntanya'], ['–', 'Tunnel statistics panel']] },
  { date: 'Dec 2023', title: 'The news box', items: [['+', '“Novetats” box: what changed since last time'], ['~', 'Boring speed 200 → 180 m a month'], ['~', 'New arrival date at Mandri']] },
  { date: 'Jul 2024', title: 'Arrival', items: [['~', 'Bored tunnel reaches Mandri'], ['~', 'Arrival forecast replaced by the actual date']] },
  { date: 'Dec 2024', title: 'Four lines', items: [['+', 'L4 and L2 join the title'], ['+', 'L2 extension from Sant Antoni to Parc Logístic'], ['–', 'Muntanya station'], ['–', 'Forecast for the end of excavation'], ['~', 'Most opening years move to 2028']] },
  { date: 'Jun 2025', title: 'Waiting for a wheel', items: [['~', 'Opening years now range from 2027 to 2030'], ['~', 'Machine note: new cutting wheel, restart in the autumn']] },
];
const symbols = [
  { name: 'Station', note: 'tick on one side' },
  { name: 'Interchange', note: 'white ring' },
  { name: 'Long interchange', note: 'capsule' },
  { name: 'Terminus', note: 'bar across the line' },
  { name: 'Under construction', note: 'warning sign' },
  { name: 'Opening year', note: 'black box' },
];
const tunnel = [
  { name: 'In service', cls: 'service' },
  { name: 'Tunnel and slab finished', cls: 'slab' },
  { name: 'Bored tunnel', cls: 'bored' },
  { name: 'Not yet bored', cls: 'none' },
];
---

<SectionNav sections={[
  { id: 'top', label: 'Overview' },
  { id: 'network', label: 'The network' },
  { id: 'what-if', label: 'What if…?' },
  { id: 'works', label: 'L9/L10 works' },
  { id: 'future', label: 'Future city' },
  { id: 'valles', label: 'Beyond Barcelona' },
  { id: 'system', label: 'System' },
  { id: 'credits', label: 'End of the line' },
]} />
<div class="metro-case-study" id="top">
  <nav class="page-back" aria-label="Portfolio"><a href="/graphic-design/">← Graphic design</a></nav>

  <article>
    <header class="intro" data-reveal>
      <p class="kicker">Information design · 2020–2026</p>
      <h1>Redrawing<br />the metro.</h1>
      <svg class="title-line" viewBox="0 0 900 40" aria-hidden="true">
        <path d="M4 20 H560 L580 8 H820" pathLength="1" />
        {[120, 260, 400, 660].map((x) => <path class="t" d={`M${x} ${x > 570 ? 8 : 20} V${x > 570 ? -4 : 8}`} />)}
        <path class="t end" d="M820 -4 V20" />
      </svg>
      <ul class="bullet-row" aria-label="The twelve lines">
        {LINES.map((l, i) => <li style={`--c:${l.color};--ink:${l.ink};--i:${i}`}>{l.id}</li>)}
      </ul>
      <p class="lead">Six years of maps of Barcelona’s metro: the network as it runs, as it’s promised, and as it could be.</p>
      <p class="summary">A diagram of the whole network, redrawn as it grows. A works map for L9 and L10, updated edition by edition while the tunnel was being dug. Proposals for lines that don’t exist, and an A3 poster of the city with all of it on.</p>
      <dl class="metadata">
        <div><dt>Role</dt><dd>Research, diagram design and data tracking</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Context</dt><dd>Personal project<br />2020–2026</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Output</dt><dd>Network diagrams, seven works editions,<br />proposals and an A3 poster</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <p class="note">Independent project. Not commissioned by or affiliated with TMB, FGC or the Generalitat de Catalunya.</p>
    </header>

    <MetroTimeline />

    <!-- ── Part 1 ───────────────────────────── -->
    <section id="network" class="section">
      <div class="split">
        <div><p class="part">Part 1</p><h2>The network,<br />2020 → 2030.</h2></div>
        <div class="copy">
          <p>It started as a diagram of the network as it ran in 2020, in the visual language of Barcelona’s own maps: line colours, white interchange rings, a legend grouping TMB and FGC lines.</p>
          <p>The same artwork then became the 2030 map. Nothing moves; lines simply grow out of their old ends, and L9 and L10 finally get their middle.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <MetroNetworkGrow />
      <MetroRules />
    </section>

    <section id="what-if" class="section">
      <div class="split">
        <div><h2>What if…?</h2></div>
        <div class="copy"><p>Once the diagram existed, it became a place to test ideas. Fade the rest of the network back, highlight two lines, and redraw.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="whatifs">
        <MetroSwap />
        <MetroVia5 />
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Part 2 ───────────────────────────── -->
    <section id="works" class="section">
      <div class="split">
        <div><p class="part">Part 2</p><h2>L9/L10: the metro that’s always almost finished.</h2></div>
        <div class="copy">
          <p>L9 and L10 run at both ends of the city, but not through the middle. From June 2022, I kept one map of the works up to date: how far the boring machine had got, how much of each station was built, and when each one was expected to open.</p>
          <p>Seven editions later, the design had barely changed. The dates had.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <aside class="statement" aria-label="Lesseps station’s opening year across editions">
        <p>Forecast:</p>
        <p class="flipboard" aria-hidden="true"><span>2025</span><span>2028</span><span>2030</span></p>
        <p class="sr">2025, then 2028, then 2030.</p>
        <p class="small">Lesseps station, in three editions of the same map.</p>
      </aside>

      <MetroWorks />

      <div class="subsection split">
        <h3>Forecast vs reality.</h3>
        <div class="copy"><p>Every edition printed a forecast for the boring machine. Here they are on one timeline, against the day it actually arrived.</p></div>
      </div>
      <MetroTbm />

      <div class="subsection split">
        <h3>The dates slip.</h3>
        <div class="copy"><p>The black year boxes are the map’s most-read element. Tracked across editions, they tell their own story.</p></div>
      </div>
      <MetroSlip />

      <div class="subsection split">
        <h3>Anatomy of a station.</h3>
        <div class="copy"><p>Every station carries its whole status in one compact label. Hover a part to find it.</p></div>
      </div>
      <MetroAnatomy />

      <div class="subsection split">
        <h3>The map changes too.</h3>
        <div class="copy"><p>Small design changes followed the news: a panel removed when it went stale, a box added to say what had changed, two more lines once their works began.</p></div>
      </div>
      <ol class="changelog" data-reveal>
        {changelog.map((c, i) => (
          <li style={`--i:${i}`}>
            <span class="when">{c.date}</span>
            <div><b>{c.title}</b>
              <ul>{c.items.map(([k, t]) => <li><span class:list={['chip', { add: k === '+', del: k === '–' }]}>{k === '~' ? '±' : k}</span>{t}</li>)}</ul>
            </div>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Part 3 ───────────────────────────── -->
    <section id="future" class="section">
      <div class="split">
        <div><p class="part">Part 3</p><h2>Barcelona,<br />further ahead.</h2></div>
        <div class="copy">
          <p>The A3 poster puts every planned and proposed line on a map of the city itself: the coast, the port, the Llobregat and Besòs rivers, Montjuïc and Collserola. The schematic rules stay, but the lines now sit roughly where the city is.</p>
          <p>It also has many more stations than the diagram, so the names drop to a smaller size and bold marks the line ends and main hubs.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <MetroA3Layers />
      <div class="subsection split">
        <h3>L4 as a loop.</h3>
        <div class="copy"><p>A second artboard fades everything but two lines to test one idea: close L4 into a ring, and let L11 take over its branch.</p></div>
      </div>
      <MetroLoop />
    </section>

    <!-- ── Part 4 ───────────────────────────── -->
    <section id="valles" class="section">
      <div class="split">
        <div><p class="part">Part 4</p><h2>Beyond<br />Barcelona.</h2></div>
        <div class="copy"><p>The same approach, applied outside the city: a proposal for rail along the Riera de Caldes, with two new FGC lines meeting at Caldes de Montbui. It borrows FGC’s conventions instead: pill-shaped line badges, thicker lines and bigger type.</p></div>
      </div>
      <MetroValles />
    </section>

    <!-- ── System ───────────────────────────── -->
    <section id="system" class="section">
      <div class="split">
        <div><h2>The system.</h2></div>
        <div class="copy"><p>Twelve line colours, a handful of symbols and four tunnel states cover every Barcelona map in the series. Hover a colour to turn it over.</p></div>
      </div>
      <ul class="palette" aria-label="Line colours">
        {LINES.map((l, i) => (
          <li style={`--c:${l.color};--ink:${l.ink};--i:${i}`} tabindex="0">
            <div class="face front"><b>{l.id}</b><span>{l.color.toUpperCase()}</span></div>
            <div class="face back"><b>{l.id}</b><span>{l.ends[0]}</span><span>{l.ends[1]}</span></div>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <div class="kit">
        <ul class="symbols" aria-label="Symbols">
          {symbols.map((s, i) => (
            <li>
              <svg viewBox="0 0 120 60" aria-hidden="true">
                {i === 0 && <><path class="sy-line" d="M10 34 H110" /><path class="sy-tick" d="M60 34 V20" /></>}
                {i === 1 && <><path class="sy-line" d="M10 34 H110" /><circle class="sy-ring" cx="60" cy="34" r="12" /></>}
                {i === 2 && <><path class="sy-line" d="M10 34 H110" /><rect class="sy-ring" x="48" y="14" width="24" height="40" rx="12" /></>}
                {i === 3 && <><path class="sy-line" d="M10 34 H80" /><path class="sy-tick" d="M80 18 V50" /></>}
                {i === 4 && <><path d="M60 12 L78 44 H42 Z" fill="#ffcc00" stroke="var(--fg)" stroke-width="2" /><text x="60" y="41" text-anchor="middle" class="sy-t">!</text></>}
                {i === 5 && <><rect x="30" y="16" width="60" height="28" fill="#111" /><text x="60" y="36" text-anchor="middle" class="sy-y">2028</text></>}
              </svg>
              <b>{s.name}</b><span>{s.note}</span>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
        <ul class="tunnel" aria-label="Tunnel states">
          {tunnel.map((t) => <li><i class={t.cls}></i><span>{t.name}</span></li>)}
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="design-notes">
        <div><h3>Type</h3><p>Helvetica Neue throughout, a familiar transport face. Bold for line ends and main interchanges, regular for everything else.</p></div>
        <div><h3>Colour</h3><p>Official line colours, never used for anything else. Status gets its own colours: pale yellow and grey for the tunnel, red for architecture and for anything that changed.</p></div>
        <div><h3>Geometry</h3><p>45° and 90° angles only, and the same artwork reused from map to map, so changes between editions are real changes.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section split reflection">
      <div><h2>Drawing a network<br />that isn’t there yet.</h2></div>
      <div class="copy">
        <p>A metro map usually shows a promise already kept: every line on it runs. Most of these maps show promises instead. The 2030 diagram draws a network that doesn’t exist yet; the works map tracks the gap between that drawing and what’s under the street; the A3 goes further still.</p>
        <p>Keeping one visual language across all of them is what makes the differences readable. The same colours, ticks and rings carry a line that runs today, a tunnel being dug and a line that’s only an idea. What changes is the state: a pale band for bored tunnel, grey for not yet, and a year box that keeps moving.</p>
        <p>The works map is also a record. Each edition shows what was known at the time, so the series now shows how a forecast drifts.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <footer class="credits" id="credits">
      <div class="end-line" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 600 60"><path class="el" d="M0 30 H560" /><path class="el-bar" d="M560 10 V50" />{[80, 200, 320, 440].map((x) => <path class="el-t" d={`M${x} 30 V16`} />)}</svg>
        <p lang="ca">Final de trajecte.</p>
        <p class="translation">End of the line.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="credit-grid">
        <div>
          <p>Martí Bravo · Personal project · 2020–2026</p>
          <p class="note">Independent work. Not commissioned by, produced for or endorsed by TMB, FGC, Ferrocarrils de la Generalitat de Catalunya or the Generalitat de Catalunya. Progress figures, forecasts and opening years are as printed on each edition at the time; opening years follow the PDI 2021–2030 estimates named in the map legend. They are a historical record, not current information.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="downloads">
          <a href="/downloads/metro-network-maps.pdf" download>Network diagram ↓<span>PDF · 2 pages</span></a>
          <a href="/downloads/metro-barcelona-a3-maps.pdf" download>A3 map and studies ↓<span>PDF · 5 pages</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </footer>
    <nav class="page-back closing" aria-label="Page navigation"><a href="/graphic-design/">← Graphic design</a><a href="#top">Back to top ↑</a></nav>
  </article>
</div>

<style>
  :global(body:has(.metro-case-study) .site) { max-width:1200px; }
  .metro-case-study { font-family:var(--campaign); font-size:1rem; line-height:1.6; }
  .metro-case-study :global(img) { display:block; max-width:100%; height:auto; }
  .metro-case-study :global(h1), .metro-case-study :global(h2), .metro-case-study :global(h3) { font-family:var(--campaign); font-weight:600; letter-spacing:-.045em; margin:0; }
  .metro-case-study :global(.note), .metro-case-study :global(figcaption) { color:var(--muted); font-size:.8125rem; line-height:1.5; }
  .metro-case-study :global(figcaption) { padding-top:.7rem; }
  .page-back { display:flex; justify-content:space-between; gap:1rem; flex-wrap:wrap; padding:1rem 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border); font-size:.875rem; }
  .page-back a { text-underline-offset:5px; }

  .intro { max-width:900px; padding:clamp(2.5rem,6vw,5rem) 0 1rem; }
  .kicker, .part { font-size:.8125rem; font-weight:700; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.08em; color:#ff6600; margin:0 0 1rem; }
  h1 { font-size:clamp(3.5rem,10vw,8rem); line-height:.92; }
  .title-line { display:block; width:min(100%,720px); height:auto; margin:1.25rem 0 1.5rem; overflow:visible; }
  .title-line path { fill:none; stroke:#ff6600; stroke-width:8; stroke-linejoin:round; }
  .title-line path:first-child { stroke-dasharray:1; stroke-dashoffset:0; }
  .title-line .t { stroke-width:6; }
  .title-line .end { stroke-width:8; }
  .intro[data-armed] .title-line path:first-child { stroke-dashoffset:1; transition:stroke-dashoffset 1.6s cubic-bezier(.5,0,.2,1) .2s; }
  .intro[data-armed] .title-line .t { opacity:0; transition:opacity .3s 1.5s; }
  .intro[data-inview] .title-line path:first-child { stroke-dashoffset:0; }
  .intro[data-inview] .title-line .t { opacity:1; }
  .bullet-row { list-style:none; display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:6px; padding:0; margin:0 0 2rem; }
  .bullet-row li { display:grid; place-items:center; min-width:2.6rem; height:2.1rem; padding:0 .35rem; background:var(--c); color:var(--ink); font-weight:700; font-size:1rem; letter-spacing:-.04em; border-radius:3px; transition:transform .45s cubic-bezier(.3,1.7,.5,1) calc(.3s + var(--i) * 70ms); }
  .bullet-row li:hover { transform:translateY(-4px) rotate(-4deg); transition-delay:0s; }
  .intro[data-armed]:not([data-inview]) .bullet-row li { transform:scale(0); }
  .lead { font-size:clamp(1.25rem,2.5vw,1.65rem); line-height:1.35; max-width:40ch; letter-spacing:-.015em; margin:0 0 1rem; }
  .summary { max-width:65ch; }
  .metadata { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1.3fr 1fr 1.3fr; gap:1.5rem; border-top:1px solid var(--border); padding-top:1.5rem; margin:2rem 0 1rem; font-size:.875rem; }
  .metadata dt { color:var(--muted); margin-bottom:.35rem; }
  .metadata dd { margin:0; }

  .section { padding:clamp(3rem,7vw,6rem) 0; scroll-margin-top:2rem; }
  .section + .section { border-top:1px solid var(--border); }
  .split { display:grid; grid-template-columns:.9fr 1.1fr; gap:clamp(2rem,6vw,6rem); }
  .split > * { min-width:0; }
  h2 { font-size:clamp(2rem,4vw,3.25rem); line-height:1.06; }
  h3 { font-size:1.5rem; line-height:1.2; }
  .copy { max-width:62ch; }
  .copy p { margin:0 0 1rem; }
  .subsection { margin-top:clamp(3.5rem,7vw,5.5rem); align-items:baseline; }
  .subsection h3 { font-size:clamp(1.5rem,2.8vw,2.1rem); }

  /* shared "what if" cards */
  .whatifs { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:1.25rem; margin-top:2.5rem; }
  .whatifs :global(.whatif) { margin:0; background:var(--hover-bg); border-radius:24px; padding:1.25rem; display:flex; flex-direction:column; }
  .whatifs :global(.tag) { display:inline-block; font-size:.75rem; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:.06em; text-transform:uppercase; background:var(--fg); color:var(--bg); padding:.2rem .55rem; border-radius:999px; margin-bottom:.75rem; }
  .whatifs :global(.card-top h3) { font-size:1.375rem; margin-bottom:.5rem; }
  .whatifs :global(.card-top p) { margin:0; font-size:.9375rem; }
  .whatifs :global(.stage) { margin-top:1rem; background:var(--bg); border-radius:16px; padding:.5rem; }
  .whatifs :global(.go) { margin-top:1rem; display:inline-flex; align-items:center; gap:.5rem; border:0; background:#992f9c; color:#fff; font:inherit; font-weight:700; padding:.6rem 1.1rem; border-radius:999px; cursor:pointer; transition:transform .2s; }
  .whatifs :global(.go:hover) { transform:translateY(-2px); }
  .whatifs :global(.go .icon) { display:inline-block; transition:transform .5s cubic-bezier(.3,1.6,.5,1); }
  .whatifs :global(.go[aria-pressed="true"] .icon) { transform:rotate(180deg); }
  .whatifs :global(.note) { margin:.75rem 0 0; }

  .statement { background:#ff6600; color:#fff; border-radius:24px; padding:clamp(1.5rem,5vw,3.5rem); margin-top:2.5rem; display:grid; grid-template-columns:auto 1fr; align-items:center; gap:.25rem 1.5rem; }
  .statement p { margin:0; }
  .statement > p:first-child { font-size:clamp(1.5rem,3.5vw,2.75rem); font-weight:600; letter-spacing:-.03em; }
  .flipboard { position:relative; height:1em; font-size:clamp(3rem,10vw,7.5rem); font-weight:700; letter-spacing:-.05em; line-height:1; perspective:400px; }
  .flipboard span { position:absolute; left:0; top:0; background:#111; color:#fff; padding:.05em .18em; border-radius:6px; animation:flipyear 7.5s infinite both; opacity:0; transform-origin:center 40%; font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums; }
  .flipboard span:nth-child(2) { animation-delay:2.5s; }
  .flipboard span:nth-child(3) { animation-delay:5s; }
  @keyframes flipyear { 0% { opacity:0; transform:rotateX(-90deg); } 5%,30% { opacity:1; transform:none; } 35%,100% { opacity:0; transform:rotateX(90deg); } }
  .statement .small { grid-column:1/-1; margin-top:1.5rem; font-size:.9375rem; opacity:.9; }
  .sr { position:absolute; width:1px; height:1px; overflow:hidden; clip:rect(0 0 0 0); white-space:nowrap; }

  .changelog { list-style:none; margin:2rem 0 0; padding:0 0 0 1.5rem; position:relative; display:grid; gap:1.25rem; }
  .changelog::before { content:''; position:absolute; left:6px; top:.4rem; bottom:.4rem; width:6px; border-radius:3px; background:linear-gradient(#ff6600,#1793f3); }
  .changelog > li { position:relative; display:grid; grid-template-columns:7rem 1fr; gap:1rem; transition:opacity .5s calc(var(--i) * .1s), transform .5s calc(var(--i) * .1s); }
  .changelog > li::before { content:''; position:absolute; left:calc(-1.5rem - 1px); top:.25rem; width:20px; height:20px; border-radius:50%; background:var(--bg); border:4px solid var(--fg); box-sizing:border-box; }
  .changelog[data-armed]:not([data-inview]) > li { opacity:0; transform:translateX(-12px); }
  .when { font-weight:700; font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums; padding-left:.75rem; }
  .changelog b { display:block; font-size:1.0625rem; margin-bottom:.35rem; }
  .changelog ul { list-style:none; padding:0; margin:0; display:grid; gap:.3rem; font-size:.875rem; }
  .changelog ul li { display:flex; gap:.5rem; align-items:baseline; }
  .chip { flex:none; display:inline-grid; place-items:center; width:1.3rem; height:1.3rem; border-radius:4px; font-weight:700; font-size:.8125rem; background:var(--hover-bg); color:var(--muted); }
  .chip.add { background:#55c14f; color:#fff; }
  .chip.del { background:#e32739; color:#fff; }

  .palette { list-style:none; padding:0; margin:2.5rem 0 0; display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(6,minmax(0,1fr)); gap:.6rem; }
  .palette li { position:relative; aspect-ratio:1; perspective:700px; cursor:pointer; outline:none; }
  .face { position:absolute; inset:0; border-radius:14px; padding:.75rem; display:flex; flex-direction:column; justify-content:space-between; backface-visibility:hidden; transition:transform .6s cubic-bezier(.3,1.3,.5,1); font-size:.75rem; line-height:1.25; }
  .front { background:var(--c); color:var(--ink); }
  .back { background:var(--bg); border:3px solid var(--c); color:var(--fg); transform:rotateY(180deg); justify-content:flex-start; gap:.3rem; }
  .face b { font-size:1.6rem; letter-spacing:-.05em; }
  .back b { font-size:1rem; color:var(--c); filter:saturate(1.2); }
  .palette li:hover .front, .palette li:focus-visible .front { transform:rotateY(-180deg); }
  .palette li:hover .back, .palette li:focus-visible .back { transform:rotateY(0); }
  .kit { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr; gap:1rem; margin-top:1rem; }
